-- title:
--   Regularity of the σ-twisted reduced j⁻¹-chart of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$, of the $q$-expansion field $\mathbb{Q}(X_1(Mp))$ attached to $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$, $j \neq 0$, have Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral } j\text{-numerator series})$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $\sigma$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ such that: the Laurent expansion of $\sigma(j)$ is the image of $j(q^p)$ (substitution of $q^p$ for $q$ on exponents); $\sigma$ preserves the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ in both directions; and for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $K$ consisting exactly of the $f \in K$ with $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$ for some $x, y \in A[[q]]$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction, the subring $\sigma^{-1}(W_0) = W_0.\mathrm{comap}\,\sigma$ differs from $W_0$ and contains both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ for every $P \in A[X]$ whose reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ is nonzero. Consider the set of $r \in k((q))$ for which there are $b \in K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$ and $x, y \in A[[q]]$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction, such that the Laurent expansion of $\sigma(b)$ times the image of $y$ in $L((q))$ equals the image of $x$, and $r$ is the quotient of the images of $x$ and $y$ in $k((q))$. The conclusion is that for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of the $k$-subalgebra of $k((q))$ generated by this set, the localisation at $\mathfrak{m}$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   This is the regularity statement, on the $j^{-1}$-chart, for the reduction modulo $p$ of the $\sigma$-twisted branch of the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$: the $k$-algebra generated by the Gauss reductions of $\sigma(b)$, $b$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, is regular of dimension one at every closed point. It is used in the comparison [`ModularCurve.XOneP.chartRing_le_adjoin_gaussReductions_map_chartAlg_of_algEquiv_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.chartRing_le_adjoin_gaussReductions_map_chartAlg_of_algEquiv_x1_mul), in the analysis of the two components of the mod $p$ fibre that underlies level lowering at $p$.
